  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lead-paragraph">I like turning complex requirements into dependable, resilient software. In my day-to-day work, that means architecting distributed payment systems handling mission-critical transactional volume across global rails. In my spare time, it means crafting focused mobile utilities and experimental developer tools.</p>
    <p>I’m a Staff Software Engineer and Tech Lead at <strong>PayPal</strong> in Bengaluru, leading architecture and engineering for OpenBanking payment initiation and alternative payment integrations. My work focuses on high-availability transactional services, settlement pipelines (spanning SEPA, UK Open Banking, Paidy, and Boku), and event-driven distributed systems using Java, Spring Boot, and Apache Kafka.</p>
    <p>Prior to PayPal, I built backend microservices, data ingestion engines, and distributed platforms at <strong>AppZen</strong>, <strong>Clairvoyant</strong>, and <strong>Persistent Systems</strong>. That foundation across enterprise big data pipelines, AI-driven corporate spend audit, and high-throughput backend services shaped how I approach engineering: understand failure modes deeply, insist on transactional idempotency, and design for long-term operational clarity.</p>
    <p>I hold a Bachelor of Engineering (B.E.) in Information Technology from <strong>MIT College of Engineering, Pune</strong> (2015).</p>
    <h2>Independent Studio: Programmer Cat</h2>
    <p>Outside of large-scale financial platforms, I design and publish consumer apps and developer utilities under my independent studio, <a href="https://programmercat.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Programmer Cat</strong> <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a>. From privacy utilities to early childhood education, these projects reflect my love for building end-to-end software that solves specific everyday problems:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/work/clean-my-links/"><strong>Clean My Links</strong></a> &mdash; An Android utility that strips tracking and marketing telemetry from shared URLs before sending them.</li>
      <li><a href="/work/minku-learns/"><strong>Minku Learns</strong></a> &mdash; A distraction-free, offline learning companion for early learners (letters, numbers, and phonics).</li>
      <li><a href="/work/unknown-messenger/"><strong>Unknown Messenger</strong></a> &mdash; A frictionless Android tool to start direct WhatsApp chats without cluttering personal address books.</li>
      <li><a href="/work/autolld/"><strong>AutoLLD</strong></a> &mdash; A CLI tool utilizing AST parsing and LLMs to generate structured Low-Level Design documents directly from codebases.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can discover more apps and release updates directly at <a href="https://programmercat.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>programmercat.com</strong></a> or inspect my technical notes and architecture breakdowns in the <a href="/work/">Projects section</a>.</p>
